  "notes": "くだらない is a common word for dismissing something as worthless or stupid. Despite looking like a negative verb form, it functions as an i-adjective.\n\nEtymology: Derived from {下|くだ}る (to go down), possibly from the Edo-period phrase 「{下|くだ}らない{酒|さけ}」 (sake that doesn't come down from Kyoto, implying inferior quality).\n\nCasual contractions:\n- くだんない (very casual)\n\nCommon collocations:\n- くだらない{話|はなし} (pointless talk)\n- くだらない{質問|しつもん} (stupid question)\n- くだらない{理由|りゆう} (trivial reason)",
